WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.030
Let’s look at your wrists, hands, fingers, and nails.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.480
A wrist or finger joint may hurt, swell, or feel stiff.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.630
Swelling of a whole finger is called dactylitis.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.930
It is a painful, sausage-like swelling.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.400
It is different from swelling around just one joint.

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:28.870
These changes can make tasks like holding a cup, or doing buttons, harder.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:36.760
Nail psoriasis may cause small pits, yellow spots, or a nail lifting from its bed.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.200
Nails can also crumble.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:45.210
Nail changes and joint symptoms do not always happen together.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:53.000
An occupational therapist can teach ways to protect your joints, and to do daily tasks.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:59.490
Tell your team whether the change is in a nail, a joint, or the whole finger.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:03.490
And mention any trouble with daily tasks.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.560
Great job! Let’s review.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:11.510
Swelling of a whole finger is called dactylitis.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:16.320
Nail changes and joint symptoms do not always happen together.
